<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10499" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντί-σπαστος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>drawn in the contrary
				direction,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεφέλαι πνεύμασιν ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>H.</u>
					21.5
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>spasmodic, convulsive,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀστέων ἀδαγμὸς ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					770
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντίσπαστος</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πούς</span>), ὁ, in
			Prosody, <i>antispast,</i> a foot made up of an iambus and
			trochee, ^ - - ^, <i><span class="en">
				Heph.
				3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aristid.Quint.
				1.22
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντίφθογγος, ἀντίσπαστα
					μέλη</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
			</span></i> Trag.<i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντίσπαστα ἐφυμνεῖ πηκτίδος συγχορδίᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					412
				</span></i>
			 (unless <i>'doubly twanged',</i> of an instrument with two
			registers). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντίσπαστον: φιλήματος ὄνομα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			Subst.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντί-σπαστος</span></b> , ὁ, <i>tackle, pulley-rope,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ath.Mech.
				9.13
			</span></i>,al.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
